  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-refactor/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, so `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow` applies. The requirement obliges each skill to open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps.\n\nThe file's sections are `# Habeas refactor`, then `## Workflow`, then `## Gotchas`. `section[Habeas refactor]/section[Workflow]` is the first and only section before `Gotchas`. Nothing else, such as a rules, background or reference section, precedes it. Under the title there is only a short unheaded paragraph. It explains what evidence records and why a move needs `habeas refactor`. It is the title's preamble, not a separate section. A stricter reading would treat that paragraph as something before the workflow. The requirement's wording is about \"any other section\", so I did not count it as a gap.\n\nThe workflow is ordered steps. It is a numbered checklist, `- [ ] 1.` through `- [ ] 7.`, in the sequence they are performed: make the move, dry run, review, run, status, commit, reassess.\n\nThe requirement lists no violation queries, so there were no violation matches to judge. I found no gap.",
